<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:bg><p:bgPr><a:gradFill rotWithShape="1"><a:gsLst><a:gs pos="36000"><a:srgbClr val="357D95"/></a:gs><a:gs pos="100000"><a:schemeClr val="tx1"/></a:gs></a:gsLst><a:lin ang="6120000" scaled="1"/></a:gradFill><a:effectLst/></p:bgPr></p:bg><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{164D9EE6-9DEE-AAA6-0194-DEC5E3A61317}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="3" name="Content Placeholder 2"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{48288213-BB43-AAE3-52C3-16C8C2D42FBF}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph idx="1"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="677584" y="2140215"/><a:ext cx="11773820" cy="7119025"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchor="t"><a:normAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buFont typeface="Wingdings" panose="05000000000000000000" pitchFamily="2" charset="2"/><a:buChar char="Ø"/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>California Senate Bill 1953 (SB 1953) and the Alfred E. Alquist Hospital Facilities Seismic Safety Act</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>First required new hospitals built after 1973 to meet stringent seismic safety standards.  After the 1994 Northridge earthquake (which damaged 11 hospitals and caused $3B in hospital damages), SB 1953 was introduced and signed in September of 1994, and is now codified in California Health &amp; Safety Code.  This applies to all facilities with a general acute hospital license but does NOT apply to acute psychiatric hospital licenses.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>In this Bill, there are two performance category systems, and building must meet BOTH to be 2030 compliant.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="1" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Structural Performance Category (SPC) the building’s bones.</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>  SPC ratings run 1 through 5.  SPC-1 is “may collapse”; SPC-5 is “fully operational after a major earthquake.  By January 01, 2030, every building used for general acute care services must be a minimum SPC-3.  Building that meet SPC-4D can stay in service indefinitely without further upgrade.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" b="1" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Nonstructural Performance Category (NPC) the guts of the building.</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t> This covers medical gas piping, emergency power, water supply, HVAC ducting, anchored equipment, elevators, stairs, etc.  By January 01, 2030, every acute care building must be NPC-5, which means the systems can sustain continuous operations for 72 hours after a major earthquake.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr marL="0" indent="0"><a:buClr><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:buClr><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>There have been numerous Senate Bills pass over the years extending various deadlines.  But the most recent Senate Bills have been vetoed by Governor Newsom.  That leaves hospital facilities with a very difficult choice: (a) figure out how to pay for the necessary projects to comply with the 2030 deadline, or (b) gamble on whether or not the new Governor will sign another extension.</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" sz="1800" dirty="0"><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="bg1"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Franklin Gothic Book" panose="020B0503020102020204" pitchFamily="34" charset="0"/></a:endParaRPr></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="6" name="Picture 5"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{787D4CD5-B4EA-B4B0-F391-AAED63EEDF8E}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvPicPr><a:picLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvPicPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId2"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{28A0092B-C50C-407E-A947-70E740481C1C}"><a14:useLocalDpi xmlns:a14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2010/main" val="0"/></a:ext></a:extLst></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="13189705" y="8444090"/><a:ext cx="1448315" cy="815151"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr></p:pic><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="8" name="Title 1"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{CBC1D56D-0654-C46B-09F7-46DD58EE3609}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"><a:spLocks/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="677584" y="1440557"/><a:ext cx="8534400" cy="436881"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:effectLst/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr vert="horz" lIns="91440" tIns="45720" rIns="91440" bIns="45720" rtlCol="0" anchor="ctr"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle><a:lvl1pPr algn="l" defTabSz="670575" rtl="0" eaLnBrk="1" latinLnBrk="0" hangingPunct="1"><a:spcBef><a:spcPct val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:buNone/><a:defRPr sz="4693" kern="1200" cap="all"><a:ln w="3175" cmpd="sng"><a:noFill/></a:ln><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="tx1"/></a:solidFill><a:effectLst/><a:latin typeface="+mj-lt"/><a:ea typeface="+mj-ea"/><a:cs typeface="+mj-cs"/></a:defRPr></a:lvl1pPr><a:lvl2pPr eaLnBrk="1" hangingPunct="1"><a:defRPr><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="tx2"/></a:solidFill></a:defRPr></a:lvl2pPr><a:lvl3pPr eaLnBrk="1" hangingPunct="1"><a:defRPr><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="tx2"/></a:solidFill></a:defRPr></a:lvl3pPr><a:lvl4pPr eaLnBrk="1" hangingPunct="1"><a:defRPr><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="tx2"/></a:sol